 R Archive Network","acronym":["CRAN"]}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2024,6,12]],"date-time":"2024-06-12T00:18:06Z","timestamp":1718151486574},"description":"Hansen's (1995) Covariate-Augmented Dickey-Fuller (CADF) test. The only required argument is y, the Tx1 time series to be tested. If no stationary covariate X is passed to the procedure, then an ordinary ADF test is performed. The p-values of the test are computed using the procedure illustrated in Lupi (2009).","reference-count":1,"publisher":"The R Foundation","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"content-updated":{"date-parts":[[2017,6,2]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2008,12,29]]},"DOI":"10.32614\/cran.package.cadftest","type":"dataset","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,6,11]],"date-time":"2024-06-11T06:10:56Z","timestamp":1718086256000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["CADFtest: A Package to Perform Covariate Augmented Dickey-Fuller Unit Root Tests"],"prefix":"10.32614","author":[{"name":"Claudio Lupi","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"17266","content-created":{"date-parts":[[2008,12,29]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Lupi C (2009). \"Unit Root CADF Testing with R.\" _Journal of Statistical Software_, *32*(2), 20.","DOI":"10.18637\/jss.v032.i02"}],"container-title":["CRAN: Contributed Packages"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,6,11]],"date-time":"2024-06-11T06:12:54Z","timestamp":1718086374000},"score":28.281197,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/CRAN.R-project.org\/package=CADFtest"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2008,12,29]]},"references-count":1,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.32614\/cran.package.cadftest","published":{"date-parts":[[2008,12,29]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,10]],"date-time":"2026-09-10T06:15:38Z","timestamp":1789020938101,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":115,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2023,12,28]],"date-time":"2023-12-28T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1703721600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["myscp.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Consumer Psychology Review"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>Consumers have available to them several potential strategies they might use to evaluate a given price. Research suggests they might compare an observed price to internal reference prices (IRPs) drawn from memory. Alternatively, consumers might evaluate a price relative to external reference prices (ERPs) available in the immediate environment. Finally, a consumer might use the seller's price image (PI), the overall impression that consumers form of the price level of a store, as a heuristic to evaluate prices. This paper briefly reviews previous research on these three evaluation strategies, as well as work investigating how these strategies interact with each other. Building on previous work, these insights are organized into a framework for predicting the factors likely to influence consumers' use of each of these strategies. It is argued that the selection of a price evaluation strategy will be based on the relative accessibility and perceived diagnosticity of IRPs, ERPs, and PIs, as well as the consumers' motivations and type of judgment the consumers are making.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/arcp.1093","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,12,28]],"date-time":"2023-12-28T22:44:16Z","timestamp":1703803456000},"page":"58-74","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":9,"title":["Consumer price evaluation strategies: Internal references, external references, and price images in consumer price perception"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"7","author":[{"O